 equity market.^This includes investments in stocks and equity derivatives by foreign individuals, institutions, and funds."},{"question":"What is the significance of Foreign Portfolio Investments (FPIs) - Equity data?","answer":"FPIs are a key indicator of global investor sentiment towards the Indian stock market, reflecting the confidence of international investors in the Indian economy and its corporate sector.^FPIs are a major driver of equity markets. Their investment patterns significantly influence market trends and valuations.^Inflows and outflows of FPIs can impact the exchange rate of the Indian Rupee, as they involve the conversion of foreign currencies into INR and vice versa.^The level of FPIs reflects the impact of government policies, regulatory environment, and economic reforms on the attractiveness of the Indian equity market to foreign investors."},{"question":"How to interpret the Foreign Portfolio Investments (FPIs) - Equity data?","answer":"Analyse the trends in FPIs in equity over time to gauge the level of foreign investor interest and confidence in the Indian market.^Assess the relationship between FPI flows and the performance of the Indian equity markets, including stock indices and market capitalisation.^Evaluate which sectors are attracting more FPIs, as this can indicate sectoral growth prospects and investor preferences.^Consider the impact of FPIs on the exchange rate and subsequently on inflation, especially if significant inflows or outflows occur.^Analyse how global economic conditions, geopolitical events, and international market trends are influencing FPIs in Indian equities.^Assess the impact of changes in government policies, regulatory norms, and economic reforms on FPI trends."}],"related":[{"slug":"10-year-credit-spread-aaa-rated-bonds-g-sec","title":"Credit Spread AAA vs G-Sec (10Y)"},{"slug":"1-year-credit-spread-aaa-rated-bonds-g-sec","title":"Credit Spread AAA vs G-Sec (1Y)"},{"slug":"3-year-credit-spread-aaa-rated-bonds-g-sec","title":"Credit Spread AAA vs G-Sec (3Y)"},{"slug":"5-year-credit-spread-aaa-rated-bonds-g-sec","title":"Credit Spread AAA vs G-Sec (5Y)"},{"slug":"consumer-price-index-cpi-inflation-headline","title":"Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation- Headline"},{"slug":"crude-oil-price-indian-basket","title":"Crude Oil Price (Indian Basket)"},{"slug":"domestic-institutional-investors-diis-investment-equity","title":"Domestic Institutional Investors (DIIs) Investment - Equity"},{"slug":"gross-foreign-direct-investment-fdi","title":"Gross Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)"},{"slug":"gross-tax-revenue","title":"Gross Tax Revenue"},{"slug":"mutual-fund-aum-equity","title":"Mutual Fund AUM- Equity"},{"slug":"primary-issuances-in-equity-market","title":"Primary Issuances in Equity Market"},{"slug":"repo-rate","title":"Repo Rate"},{"slug":"usd-inr-exchange-rate","title":"USD/INR Exchange Rate"}],"title":"Foreign Portfolio Investments (FPIs) - Equity","description":"Net FPI equity flows stand at $ -3,750.2 Million for Sep 2026. This flow tends to correlate more with global risk sentiment than domestic fundamentals.","headline":{"Absolute":"Net FPI equity flows stand at $ -3,750.2 Million for Sep 2026. This flow tends to correlate more with global risk sentiment than domestic fundamentals.","Y-o-Y":"Net FPI equity flows stand at -46.95% for Jun 2025. This flow tends to correlate more with global risk sentiment than domestic fundamentals."},"source":"CMIE Economic Outlook, 1 Finance Research","source_url":"https://economicoutlook.cmie.com/","date_modified":"2026-09-01","scraped_at":"2026-10-13T15:28:05+00:00"}